t":[{"type":"text","text":"      Tests  12 passed | 29 todo (41)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784907458464},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm verifying the premium calculation logic—first insurance applies as a 10% surcharge on the base premium, while curse surcharge is 50% of the item base, and these are both added separately to reach the total. The curse surcharge isn't affected by first insurance, so the formula holds correctly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Green Phase Complete: 12 passing.\n\n## Green -- cursed item surcharge (50% of item base premium)"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01C9SxXGKa9H4Wjhq4A8nw4q","name":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 12\nRecent changes: Added item-level curse surcharge (50% of that item's base premium) as an additive modifier. Premium = ceil(base*1.1 + itemSurcharges) + 5 fee. Added helpers itemSurcharge and itemInsuredBasePremium; added cursed?: boolean to Item.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Note: more modifiers coming (high enchantment 30%, loyalty 20% discount, follow-up 15% discount) which will need to compose additively per the spec's modifier-scope rule.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":957,"output":573,"cacheRead":51793,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":53323,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784907458466,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-e0306c4e-ab3e-4fe2-a6a7-7dc3e84f62eb","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01C9SxXGKa9H4Wjhq4A8nw4q","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 12 tests still green.\n\n## Refactoring Report\n\n**Refactoring Applied**: Restructured `quotePremiumForStep` to express **first-insurance as an additive surcharge** rather than a multiplicative factor.\n\n### Step 5: Refactored Code Mass\n\n```typescript\nconst basePremium = basePremiumForItems(step.items);\nconst firstInsuranceSurcharge = basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE;\nconst itemSurcharges = step.items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + itemSurcharge(item), 0);\nconst modifiedPremium = basePremium + firstInsuranceSurcharge + itemSurcharges;\nconst premium = Math.ceil(roundCents(modifiedPremium)) + PROCESSING_FEE;\nreturn { premium };\n```\n\nMass is essentially unchanged (~34 → ~35; one extra `+` invocation and binding). **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) trumps APP** here — the negligible mass increase buys correct, extensible modifier semantics.\n\n### Step 6: Decision Rationale\n\n- **Naming (Rule 2, first priority)**: `FIRST_INSURANCE_MULTIPLIER = 1.1` (a multiplicative full-value factor) was renamed to `FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1` (an additive rate), and the intermediate `withFirstInsurance` became `firstInsuranceSurcharge`. The old name hid that first-insurance is *one additive modifier among several*.\n- **Composition correctness**: The new `modifiedPremium = base + firstInsuranceSurcharge + itemSurcharges` makes all modifiers compose **additively on the base**, exactly matching the spec's modifier-scope rule. The upcoming modifiers (high-enchantment 30%, loyalty 20% discount, follow-up 15% discount) now slot in as additional `± base * rate` surcharge/discount terms in the same sum — no structural change needed.\n- **Rule 3 (DRY)**: First-insurance and curse now share the \"surcharge = base × rate\" shape, revealing the shared concept instead of two different mechanisms.\n- **Rule 1 (Tests)**: All 12 tests remain green (arithmetically identical: `base * 1.1` ≡ `base + base * 0.1`).\n\n### Step 7: Completion\n\n- **Refactoring**: First-insurance reframed as an additive rate-based surcharge; renamed constant and intermediate variable for intent.\n- **Mass Change**: ~34 → ~35 (Rule 2 clarity intentionally chosen over marginal APP)\n- **Tests**: All 12 passing."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-2/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 12\nRecent changes: Added item-level curse surcharge (50% of that item's base premium) as an additive modifier. Premium = ceil(base*1.1 + itemSurcharges) + 5 fee. Added helpers itemSurcharge and itemInsuredBasePremium; added cursed?: boolean to Item.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Note: more modifiers coming (high enchantment 30%, loyalty 20% discount, follow-up 15% discount) which will need to compose additively per the spec's modifier-scope rule.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 12\nRecent changes: Added item-level curse surcharge (50% of that item's base premium) as an additive modifier. Premium = ceil(base*1.1 + itemSurcharges) + 5 fee. Added helpers itemSurcharge and itemInsuredBasePremium; added cursed?: boolean to Item.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Note: more modifiers coming (high enchantment 30%, loyalty 20% discount, follow-up 15% discount) which will need to compose additively per the spec's modifier-scope rule.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784907466890},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm examining the current implementation and its test coverage.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01DqCe1sP1u5gGmvYnKGQnm4","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-2/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01JEKbbXqcyTuXCx1igABJtf","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-2/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":328,"output":253,"cacheRead":9696,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10277,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784907466910,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ab4a38d1-3b04-4545-9a22-bef206c64d58","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01DqCe1sP1u5gGmvYnKGQnm4","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Item {\n  type: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface Step {\n  op: string;\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\nexport interface StepResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nexport interface ScenarioResult {\n  results: StepResult[];\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_MULTIPLIER = 1.1;\n\nexport const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult => {\n  const results = scenario.steps.map(quotePremiumForStep);\n  return { results };\n};\n\nconst quotePremiumForStep = (step: Step): StepResult => {\n  const basePremium = basePremiumForItems(step.items);\n  const itemSurcharges = step.items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + itemSurcharge(item),\n    0\n  );\n  const withFirstInsurance = basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_MULTIPLIER;\n  const premium =\n    Math.ceil(roundCents(withFirstInsurance + itemSurcharges)) + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return { premium };\n};\n\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst itemSurcharge = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = itemInsuredBasePremium(item);\n  return item.cursed ? base * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n};\n\nconst itemInsuredBasePremium = (item: Item): number =>\n  isComponent(item) ? COMPONENT_UNIT_PREMIUM : basePremiumForItem(item);\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst COMPONENT_UNIT_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst isComponent = (item: Item): boolean => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type);\n\nconst basePremiumForItems = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const components = items.filter(isComponent);\n  const mainItems = items.filter((item) => !isComponent(item));\n  const mainTotal = mainItems.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + basePremiumForItem(item),\n    0\n  );\n  return mainTotal + componentsBasePremium(components);\n};\n\nconst componentsBasePremium = (components: Item[]): number => {\n  const countByType = countComponentsByType(components);\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const count of countByType.values()) {\n    total += componentGroupPremium(count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst countComponentsByType = (components: Item[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const countByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const component of components) {\n    countByType.set(component.type, (countByType.get(component.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return countByType;\n};\n\nconst componentGroupPremium = (count: number): number => {\n  if (count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE) return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n  return count * COMPONENT_UNIT_PREMIUM;\n};\n\nconst roundCents = (n: number): number => Math.round(n * 100) / 100;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (item: Item): number =>\n  BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE[item.type] ?? BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE.sword;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784907469694},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01JEKbbXqcyTuXCx1igABJtf","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { runScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // --- Simplest / edge ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 5 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Base premiums per main item (base + fee, newcomer adds first-insurance) ---\n  // We isolate base premium behaviour using a long-standing? No: newcomer has first-insurance surcharge.\n  // Keep base-premium tests via multi-modifier integration; but list per-item base values.\n  it(\"single sword base premium 100 G\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    // base 100 + 10% first insurance (10) + 5 fee = 115\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"single amulet base premium 60 G\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    // 60 + 10% first insurance (6) + 5 fee = 71\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"single staff base premium 80 G\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    // 80 + 10% (8) + 5 = 93\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 93 });\n  });\n  it(\"single potion base premium 40 G\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    // 40 + 10% (4) + 5 = 49\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 49 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Components and building blocks ---\n  it(\"2 runes -> 50 G base premium\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    // base 2*25 = 50; +10% (5) + 5 fee = 60\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 60 });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> 60 G base premium (block applies)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    // block of 3 alike -> base 60; +10% (6) + 5 fee = 71\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> 100 G base premium (no block, requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    const items = Array(4).fill({ type: \"rune\" });\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items }],\n    });\n    // 4 runes = 100 base (no block); +10% (10) + 5 = 115\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes -> 175 G base premium\", () => {\n    const items = Array(7).fill({ type: \"rune\" });\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items }],\n    });\n    // 7 runes = 175 base (no block, only exactly-3 blocks); +10% (17.5)=192.5 ceil + 5 = 198\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 198 });\n  });\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> 75 G base premium (no block: different types)\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    // no block (types differ): 3*25 = 75 base; +10% (7.5)=82.5 ceil 83 + 5 = 88\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 88 });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> 120 G base premium (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    const items = [\n      ...Array(3).fill({ type: \"rune\" }),\n      ...Array(3).fill({ type: \"moonstone\" }),\n    ];\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items }],\n    });\n    // two blocks: 60 + 60 = 120 base; +10% (12) + 5 = 137\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 137 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Premium modifiers in isolation ---\n  it(\"cursed sword adds 50% risk surcharge of item base premium\", () => {\n    const result = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }] },\n      ],\n    });\n    // base 100 + curse (50% of item base = 50) + first insurance (10% of policy base 100 = 10) = 160; +5 fee = 165\n    expect(result.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 165 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"highly enchanted item (enchantment >= 5) adds 30% surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"long-standing customer (>= 2 years) receives 20% loyalty discount\");\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years -> loyalty discount applies\");\n  it.todo(\"first insurance carries 10% initial assessment surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"follow-up contract (each after first) gets 15% discount\");\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword + plain amulet -> 210 G before further modifiers and fee (curse applies to item base only)\");\n\n  // --- Rounding ---\n  it.todo(\"premium yielding 197.5 G -> final premium 198 G (rounded up)\");\n  it.todo(\"payout yielding 350.5 G -> final payout 350 G (rounded down)\");\n\n  // --- Integration examples