, `componentGroupPremium` — all reveal intent well.\n- The recently changed `itemSurcharge` now contains an inline expression `(item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD` whose *intent* (\"is this item highly enchanted?\") is not named. Extracting a predicate `isHighlyEnchanted` would reveal intent — mirroring the existing well-named `isComponent`. **Decision: extract `isHighlyEnchanted`.**\n\n**Step 2: Initial APP Mass — `itemSurcharge`**\n\n```ts\nconst itemSurcharge = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = itemInsuredBasePremium(item);\n  let surcharge = 0;\n  if (item.cursed) surcharge += base * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD)\n    surcharge += base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE;\n  return surcharge;\n};\n```\n- Constants: `0`, `0` = 2\n- Bindings: base(3), surcharge(4), item(3), CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE, HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD, HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE = 13\n- Invocations: itemInsuredBasePremium(2), `*`×2(4), `??`(2), `>=`(2) = 10\n- Conditionals: 2 `if` = 8\n- Assignments: `let surcharge = 0`(6), `+=`×2(12) = 18\n\n**Total Mass: 51**\n\n**Step 3: Apply Simple Design Rules**\n\n- Rule 2 (Intent): unnamed threshold check → extract `isHighlyEnchanted`.\n- Rule 3 (Duplication): both branches share the `base * rate` shape → collect into a single rate sum, removing the mutable accumulator.\n\nApplying both:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01GkgsD4GEv6eqXztv4StcRz","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edit\n":"\n<parameter name=\"edits\">[{\"oldText\": \"const itemSurcharge = (item: Item): number => {\\n  const base = itemInsuredBasePremium(item);\\n  let surcharge = 0;\\n  if (item.cursed) surcharge += base * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD)\\n    surcharge += base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE;\\n  return surcharge;\\n};\", \"newText\": \"const itemSurcharge = (item: Item): number => {\\n  const surchargeRate =\\n    (item.cursed ? CURSE_